<title>SWITZERLAND: SMH says Swatch sales jumped in U.S..</title>
<headline>SMH says Swatch sales jumped in U.S..</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss watchmaker Ste Suisse Microelectronique et d'Horlogerie SA (SMH) said sales of its Swatch watches in the United States rose sharply in 1995 and 1996, contrary to a newspaper report that they had fallen.</p>
<p>The company said sales in the U.S. rose 22 percent by volume and 24 percent by revenue in 1996 after increasing 51 percent by volume and 54 percent in revenue terms in 1995.</p>
<p>SMH bearer shares closed down 11 Swiss francs at 952.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
